WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.119
The pirates’ ship was indeed very interesting.

2
00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:07.400
In every room, the animals found something new.

3
00:00:07.401 --> 00:00:10.669
"Look at this bed!" Gub-Gub jumped on it.

4
00:00:10.670 --> 00:00:14.427
"The pillows and blanket are silk!"

5
00:00:14.428 --> 00:00:16.994
Dab-Dab opened the closet.

6
00:00:16.995 --> 00:00:19.043
He tried on the slippers.

7
00:00:19.044 --> 00:00:20.913
They wouldn’t fit.

8
00:00:20.914 --> 00:00:23.386
"WOW! Look at this!"

9
00:00:23.387 --> 00:00:26.783
Dab-Dab pulled out a large pirate’s hat.

10
00:00:26.784 --> 00:00:30.518
"I am the Great Barbary . . . DUCK!"

11
00:00:30.519 --> 00:00:34.677
Dab-Dab said in a low voice.

12
00:00:34.678 --> 00:00:36.625
There was so much to see.

13
00:00:36.626 --> 00:00:40.645
In one room, they found gold, silver, and jewels.

14
00:00:40.646 --> 00:00:42.939
It was the pirates’ treasure.

15
00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:48.675
"Dr. Dolittle won’t have to worry about money anymore," said Gub-Gub.

16
00:00:48.676 --> 00:00:51.412
"Don’t touch it!" snapped Jip.

17
00:00:51.413 --> 00:00:54.296
"The pirates stole this from people."

18
00:00:54.297 --> 00:00:58.107
"We can’t return it," Gub-Gub rubbed his hand.

19
00:00:58.108 --> 00:01:00.997
"But it’s not ours!" growled Jip.

20
00:01:00.998 --> 00:01:03.630
"Don’t touch it!"

21
00:01:03.631 --> 00:01:07.695
Dab-Dab found a door he couldn’t open.

22
00:01:07.696 --> 00:01:11.597
"I wonder what’s behind this door?" he asked.

23
00:01:11.598 --> 00:01:14.870
The others came over and tried to open it.

24
00:01:14.871 --> 00:01:18.283
"Maybe it’s more treasures," guessed Gub-Gub.

25
00:01:18.284 --> 00:01:20.772
Dab-Dab’s eyes got big.

26
00:01:20.773 --> 00:01:28.975
"Maybe . . . maybe . . . the pirates put bodies in there."

27
00:01:28.976 --> 00:01:32.415
Dr. Dolittle was enjoying a quiet moment.

28
00:01:32.416 --> 00:01:34.993
He was thinking about the monkeys.

29
00:01:34.994 --> 00:01:38.677
He was thinking about Polynesia and Chee-Chee.

30
00:01:38.678 --> 00:01:41.276
And he was thinking about Puddleby.

31
00:01:41.277 --> 00:01:47.339
"DR. DOLITTLE!" All the animals started talking at once.

32
00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:52.711
"Slow down! I can’t understand any of you," the doctor said.

33
00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:54.500
Jip spoke first.

34
00:01:54.501 --> 00:01:58.359
"We found a room, but the door is locked."

35
00:01:58.360 --> 00:02:03.600
"We think," gulped Dab-Dab, "there are bodies inside."

36
00:02:03.601 --> 00:02:08.451
"Bodies?" the doctor said, alarmed.

37
00:02:08.453 --> 00:02:12.227
Dr. Dolittle followed the animals to the locked room.

38
00:02:12.228 --> 00:02:16.883
"Oh, my! Look at all this gold!" he remarked.

39
00:02:16.884 --> 00:02:21.200
"Over here, Doctor!" Dab-Dab pointed to the door.

40
00:02:21.201 --> 00:02:25.579
"Well, let’s see if we can find the key," said the doctor.

41
00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:29.333
Everyone started to look for a key.

42
00:02:29.334 --> 00:02:33.102
While they were looking, Too-Too suddenly said:

43
00:02:33.103 --> 00:02:35.114
"There’s someone inside."

44
00:02:35.115 --> 00:02:37.626
Everyone became silent.

45
00:02:37.627 --> 00:02:41.201
"I don’t hear anything, Too-Too," said the doctor.

46
00:02:41.202 --> 00:02:44.585
But Too-Too was listening.

47
00:02:44.586 --> 00:02:46.317
"There it is again!

48
00:02:46.318 --> 00:02:48.176
Don’t you hear that?"

49
00:02:48.177 --> 00:02:51.031
But nobody could hear a thing.

50
00:02:51.032 --> 00:02:54.046
Too-Too leaned closer against the door.

51
00:02:54.047 --> 00:02:57.622
"What do you hear?" asked Jip.

52
00:02:57.623 --> 00:03:02.377
"Someone is putting their hands in their pockets," replied the owl.

53
00:03:02.378 --> 00:03:05.778
The others looked at each other and smiled.

54
00:03:05.779 --> 00:03:07.649
"How can you hear that?

55
00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:13.975
That doesn’t make any sound at all," giggled Dab-Dab.

56
00:03:13.976 --> 00:03:17.106
Too-Too gave Dab-Dab a long stare.

57
00:03:17.107 --> 00:03:19.754
"We owls have very good ears.

58
00:03:19.755 --> 00:03:24.621
Besides, everything makes a sound," Too-Too explained.

59
00:03:24.622 --> 00:03:28.138
"How interesting," said the doctor.

60
00:03:28.139 --> 00:03:30.285
"What’s he doing now?"

61
00:03:30.286 --> 00:03:34.071
"He’s rubbing his face," Too-Too reported.

62
00:03:34.072 --> 00:03:35.314
"It’s a woman.

63
00:03:35.315 --> 00:03:39.190
NO! It’s a man."

64
00:03:39.191 --> 00:03:41.039
Dab-Dab was right.

65
00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:43.627
There was a body inside the room.

66
00:03:43.628 --> 00:03:45.978
Except it wasn’t dead.

67
00:03:45.979 --> 00:03:48.167
It was still alive.

68
00:03:48.168 --> 00:03:51.606
Too-Too looked through the lock for a long time.

69
00:03:51.607 --> 00:03:54.519
"The man inside is very sad.

70
00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:57.714
He is crying," he said finally.

71
00:03:57.715 --> 00:04:04.628
"Then let’s help him get out!" said the doctor.

